<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS10.SSS3.P1" title="In 4.10.3 Possible Designs ‣ 4.10 Software Engineering Agent ‣ 4 Case Studies ‣ Design Patterns for Securing LLM Agentsagainst Prompt Injections" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">1) </span>Base agent with user confirmation.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS10.SSS3.P2" title="In 4.10.3 Possible Designs ‣ 4.10 Software Engineering Agent ‣ 4 Case Studies ‣ Design Patterns for Securing LLM Agentsagainst Prompt Injections" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">2) </span>Action-sandboxing.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS10.SSS3.P3" title="In 4.10.3 Possible Designs ‣ 4.10 Software Engineering Agent ‣ 4 Case Studies ‣ Design Patterns for Securing LLM Agentsagainst Prompt Injections" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">3) </span>Dual LLM with strict data formatting.</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
</ol></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_section"><a href="#S5" title="In Design Patterns for Securing LLM Agentsagainst Prompt Injections" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">5 </span>Conclusions &amp; Recommendations</span></a></li>
